Package: penalties7
Title: Penalties as Objects with Exact Derivatives
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
    person("Giovanni", "Tinervia", , "giovannitinervia9@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Penalties for regularized and Bayesian regression as 'S7'
    objects: a linear map, a scalar function and hyperparameters, with the
    value, the exact derivatives in the coefficients and in the
    hyperparameters, the mixed block, and, for quadratic penalties, the
    rank, the null space and the log pseudo-determinant that a marginal
    likelihood criterion consumes. Normalizing constants are kept, so a
    proper penalty is exactly the negative log-density of its prior.
    Part of the 'statmodels7' toolkit.
